+    <string name="bare_whats_new_205_settings" translatable="false">Settings are tidier: Address bar &amp; toolbar, Look &amp; feel, and an About page with Bare and Chromium versions.</string>
+    <string name="bare_whats_new_205_shortcuts" translatable="false">New tab shortcuts sit in a 4 by 2 grid that scrolls, with room for 16.</string>
+    <string name="bare_whats_new_205_downloads" translatable="false">Downloads fetch in parts, pause and resume later, can go to a folder you choose, and show live progress.</string>
+    <string name="bare_whats_new_205_games" translatable="false">No internet? Play Bare Fly, Bare Run or Bare Racer, or open bare://games any time.</string>
+    <string name="bare_whats_new_205_bareurl" translatable="false">Type bare:// to open Bare\'s own pages, like bare://flags.</string>
+    <string name="bare_whats_new_205_smoothoff" translatable="false">Smooth scrolling is now off by default, so scrolling feels like Chrome on a phone.</string>
+    <string name="bare_whats_new_205_barhide" translatable="false">On a new tab, the bar hides as soon as you scroll.</string>
+    <string name="bare_whats_new_208_languages">Bare now speaks ten more languages.</string>
+    <string name="bare_whats_new_208_rtl">In Arabic and other right-to-left languages, the vertical tabs drawer now opens from the right and the bars are mirrored.</string>
+    <string name="bare_whats_new_208_backbtn">The back button on the address bar is off by default. To bring it back, turn on Back button on the address bar in Settings &gt; Appearance &gt; Address bar &amp; toolbar.</string>
+    <string name="bare_whats_new_208_chromium">Built on Chromium 158.0.8127.42.</string>
+    <string name="bare_whats_new_209_siteicon">The site icon is back on secure pages. Tap it to see the site\'s settings.</string>
+    <string name="bare_whats_new_209_video">Download video on a long press now saves the video you pressed, with its sound.</string>
+    <string name="bare_whats_new_209_card">Downloads ask where to save the file, so you can pick a folder before they start.</string>
+    <string name="bare_whats_new_209_progress">A download\'s progress shows briefly inside the address bar.</string>
+    <string name="bare_whats_new_209_loading">The line that shows a page loading now runs inside the address bar.</string>
+    <string name="bare_whats_new_209_filetype">Downloads get the right file type, so they open with the right app.</string>
+    <string name="bare_whats_new_209_1dm">Downloads sent to apps like 1DM now keep your sign-in and the file name.</string>
+    <string name="bare_whats_new_209_downloadspage">On the Downloads page, a long press on a file opens its menu, deleting asks first, and tapping a video plays it in Bare Player.</string>
+    <string name="bare_whats_new_209_welcome">The welcome pages and the backup setup pages are tidier.</string>
+    <string name="bare_whats_new_209_switch">You can turn this page off in Settings &gt; About, with Show What\'s new after updates.</string>
+    <string name="bare_whats_new_209_chromium">Built on Chromium 158.0.8127.42.</string>
+    <string name="bare_whats_new_207_crx" translatable="false">Adding extensions from the Chrome Web Store, or from a .crx link, works again.</string>
+    <string name="bare_whats_new_207_center" translatable="false">The address is centered again in the address bar when you are not typing.</string>
+    <string name="bare_whats_new_207_downloads" translatable="false">Downloads no longer crash on some Android 16 phones.</string>
+    <string name="bare_whats_new_207_ellipsis" translatable="false">A site name that is too long for the address bar now keeps its start and ends in an ellipsis, instead of losing its first letters.</string>
+    <string name="bare_whats_new_206_toolbar" translatable="false">The toolbar folds away when you scroll even with TalkBack or another accessibility service on. To keep it on screen, turn on Keep toolbar visible.</string>
+    <string name="bare_whats_new_206_crash" translatable="false">Fixed a crash that could happen with the address bar at the bottom.</string>
